    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n63302" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λῐμηρός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιμήν</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>furnished with a good
				harbour</i>, special epith. of Epidaurus in Laconia, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				4.56
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.26
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐλίμενον δὲ οὖσαν, βραχέως . .
					λιμηρὰν εἰρῆσθαι, ὡς ἂν λιμενηράν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Apollod.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				8.6.1
			</span></i>.</div>
